   "text": "Fox School of Business - Temple University - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nFox School of Business - Temple University\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nThe Fox School of Business at Temple University has a distinguished tradition of preparing business leaders, professionals and entrepreneurs for successful careers. It is the largest, most comprehensive business school in the greater Philadelphia region.\nThoroughly committed to providing student-centered education and professional development relevant to today’s digital, global economy — the Fox School integrates technology into the curriculum and classroom, and encourages entrepreneurship and innovation throughout its programs.\nThe Fox School’s global presence, perspective, and strategic alliances with regional and international business communities position students among dominant and growth industries in financial services, healthcare, information technology, pharmaceuticals/biotechnology, and tourism and hospitality.\nTimestamps\nUpdated\n26/03/2026 08:06\nby Gunia Beniwal\nCreated\n26/03/2026 08:06\nby Gunia Beniwal\nType\nUniversity\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\nCountry\nUnited States\nYearly Fees\nMax: US$30,000.00\nMin: US$19,800.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n0%\n0 of 599 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPublic\nProvider\nDirect QS\nFounded Year\n1918\nCampus(es)\nPhiladelphia\nCountry\nUnited States\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n Yes\nContract Start Date\n26/01/2023\nContract End Date\n01/01/2036\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\nhttps://www.fox.temple.edu/news/2022/11/leaving-nest-what-know-when-looking-campus-housing\nScholarship Offered\n*Merit-based scholarships are available and reviewed at the time of application.\n*There is no guaranteed minimum GPA for merit-based scholarships, but generally, a GPA \n of around 3.3 or higher is recommended.\n*The amount of scholarships varies, with a typical range of $1,000 to $5,000.\nhttps://www.fox.temple.edu/academics/advising/awards-scholarships\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/user/foxwebvideos\nInternship Details\nhttps://www.fox.temple.edu/students/parents-families/internships-careers\nAdditional Information\n-",
